parliament will set out its position on  the digital green certificate which aims  to facilitate a return to eu  travel it would allow people to prove a  negative test or immunity from covid19  meps will set out their red lines  including not discriminating against  people who haven't been vaccinated  parliament will vote on the ratification  of the trade and cooperation agreement  cementing a new partnership with the uk  meps will reiterate their calls for the  uk to stand by its commitments in the  withdrawal agreement  especially concerning northern ireland  the pandemic has shown that research and  innovation have never been so important  parliament will vote on the 95 billion  euro horizon europe program  investing in research across the eu from  preparing for future health threats  to helping the transition towards  climate neutrality  meps will vote on new rules to prevent  the dissemination of terrorist content  online  the proposals include a europe-wide  legal definition of terrorist material  and oblige platforms to remove illegal  content within one hour  parliament will vote on rules to improve  the experience of train users  the new legislation provides for better  compensation and help in case of delays  more space on trains for bikes and  easier access for the disabled
 

